  "upstream_repository": "https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf",
  "upstream_commit": "fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643",
  "upstream_component_path": "components/fatfs",
  "upstream_component_worktree_clean": true,
  "fatfs_revision": "R0.16 / FF_DEFINED80386",
  "patches": [
    "Enable official FatFs GPT scanner via FF_LBA64=1 and its required FF_FS_EXFAT=1; preserve LFN and physical512-byte SD geometry",
    "Retain IDF/managed MSC uint32 sector driver ABI with checked LBA64 read/write and GET_SECTOR_COUNT/CTRL_TRIM adapters in diskio.c",
    "Use owned local generation helpers from project_include.cmake rather than an installed SDK path",
    "Normalize disabled CONFIG_FATFS_USE_LABEL to FF_USE_LABEL=0 in C expressions reached by the enabled official exFAT path; retain label feature disabled",
    "Reject sizes, transfers and seeks outside signed libc VFS off_t/ssize_t bounds before64bit FatFs operations; preserve safe negative seeks and EOF reads",
    "Retain generic VFS callback context on esp_vfs_unregister failure; BDL unmount preserves diskio/context until checked unregister succeeds",
    "SD unmount retains card/context/diskio on VFS failure, tracks completed VFS stage and latches nontransactional host-deinit errors without unsafe repeat",
    "Clear released SD drive/card bindings on mount cleanup and unmount to prevent stale card-address/pdrv aliasing with USB; lookup partition context by base path",
    "Preallocate SD cleanup-owner context before VFS mount publication rather than failing a late owner allocation after successful mount",
    "Project-authored timed shared lifecycle mutex serializes TF/USB whole mount/unmount transactions without locking ordinary per-volume file IO"
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Underlying IDF SD/MMC and MSC drivers retain32-bit sector/count contracts; out-of-range requests are explicitly refused",
    "All consumers must rebuild against this one FatFs header/structure ABI; never mix installed-SDK ff.h with local fatfs sources",
    "Actual user media is not formatted or modified by compatibility diagnosis/tests",
    "ESP32-S31 application VFS off_t/st_size is signed32bit; nonrepresentable file sizes/offsets are rejected with EOVERFLOW rather than expanded or truncated",
    "A failed SD or MSC host/device teardown can be nontransactional; retain ownership and require hardware reset rather than retrying partially freed driver objects",
    "Compound mount failure plus VFS-unregister rollback failure is not fully transactional in the inherited SDK mount error API and is not qualified by these cleanup tests"
  ],
  "license_sha256": "cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30",
